            <ArticleTitle>Chronic abdominal pain and upper gastrointestinal bleeding due to duodenal perforation caused by migrated inferior vena cava filter--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe an unusual case of a 41-year-old man presenting with chronic abdominal pain and gastrointestinal bleeding caused by a migrated inferior vena cava filter eroding into the duodenum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
